WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.617 --> 00:00:03.835
♪ driving rock ♪

00:00:03.853 --> 00:00:05.453
Absolutely stunning.

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.622
Because you'll see
way more of it in Europe.

00:00:07.622 --> 00:00:09.274
Didn't expect to see that here either.

00:00:09.506 --> 00:00:10.885
Oh, we're still not there.

00:00:10.927 --> 00:00:12.177
Sorry, it's my judgmental nature.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:14.934
I haven't seen that part of the city yet.

00:00:14.934 --> 00:00:16.432
-Oh, you should go there.
-I should.

00:00:17.641 --> 00:00:18.562
Pumped.

00:00:18.562 --> 00:00:19.562
Yay!

00:00:21.186 --> 00:00:22.866
Here in Kyiv, Ukraine

00:00:23.203 --> 00:00:25.780
and about to go
to the far west of the country

00:00:25.823 --> 00:00:27.741
to a city called Lviv.

00:00:27.988 --> 00:00:32.654
I've been told it's
like a very European city.

00:00:32.684 --> 00:00:34.124
♪ upbeat choir chanting ♪

00:01:20.057 --> 00:01:21.097
[music fades]

00:01:21.183 --> 00:01:25.184
Feels like a much different
Ukraine than Kyiv

00:01:26.151 --> 00:01:28.270
or the other parts
of the country I've seen.

00:01:28.696 --> 00:01:29.736
♪ indy rock ♪

00:01:31.925 --> 00:01:33.271
People have always told me

00:01:33.271 --> 00:01:36.117
"Lviv is way more European feeling."

00:01:36.117 --> 00:01:38.412
and sure, yeah, it is... Definitely.

00:01:38.412 --> 00:01:41.543
And coming from Kyiv,
well it's obviously smaller.

00:01:41.543 --> 00:01:45.075
There was immediately
this chill, relaxed

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:48.583
sort of melodic-type feel to the place.

00:01:49.191 --> 00:01:51.591
Everyone hanging out in the squares.

00:01:52.326 --> 00:01:54.193
So there are a ton of cafes

00:01:54.432 --> 00:01:56.032
a lot of restaurants

00:01:56.565 --> 00:01:59.096
and a lot of interesting spaces here.

00:01:59.488 --> 00:02:01.308
Like a lot of well thought out design.

00:02:02.775 --> 00:02:04.538
[music continues]

00:02:05.753 --> 00:02:08.171
Craft beer, craft chocolate.

00:02:11.407 --> 00:02:13.360
There are all sort of craft products.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.996
So I feel like there's a lot of pride
in the people here, in the culture.

00:02:18.996 --> 00:02:20.036
[music fades]

00:02:30.563 --> 00:02:32.872
Very good.
Very, very good coffee shop

00:02:32.872 --> 00:02:36.470
and I met this unlucky victim, Ivan.

00:02:36.529 --> 00:02:38.003
♪ indy rock ♪

00:02:41.719 --> 00:02:43.058
SOLOMIA: We love you.

00:02:46.283 --> 00:02:47.412
Tell me about this city.

00:02:47.412 --> 00:02:48.463
I just go here.

00:02:48.463 --> 00:02:50.951
You feel like
you're always in the city center.

00:02:50.951 --> 00:02:52.783
Like life is always around us.

00:02:52.783 --> 00:02:56.172
There is always something 'cause
there are plenty of festivals every day

00:02:56.172 --> 00:02:58.480
but you just feel like
you're part of something big.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.160
Like part of great party.

00:03:00.417 --> 00:03:01.745
-Really?
-Yeah, seriously, yeah.

00:03:01.811 --> 00:03:03.011
♪ traditional ♪

00:03:05.953 --> 00:03:07.614
♪ alternative rock ♪

00:03:10.007 --> 00:03:11.607
♪ electronic dance ♪

00:03:25.861 --> 00:03:27.061
♪ traditional ♪

00:03:34.043 --> 00:03:35.813
And there's a ton of art in this city.

00:03:35.813 --> 00:03:37.880
There's art all over the place.

00:03:39.497 --> 00:03:40.849
Lot of street music.

00:03:40.882 --> 00:03:44.032
-Good local music scene?
-Yeah, pretty good.

00:03:44.032 --> 00:03:45.057
Lot of musicians.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:47.092
Just to come over here
and listen to some music.

00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:48.092
Right.

00:03:48.141 --> 00:03:49.341
♪ traditional ♪

00:03:58.172 --> 00:03:59.852
♪ busker playing guitar ♪

00:04:01.853 --> 00:04:03.293
♪ emotional rock ♪

00:04:20.746 --> 00:04:21.786
[music fades]

00:04:27.884 --> 00:04:29.364
[light rain]

00:04:36.518 --> 00:04:38.198
I like the texture here

00:04:38.664 --> 00:04:42.785
and even if some of these buildings
are falling apart a little on the outside

00:04:42.785 --> 00:04:44.519
you can see the structure

00:04:45.232 --> 00:04:47.883
the craft, the thought, the design

00:04:47.883 --> 00:04:49.563
the beauty behind them.

00:04:49.712 --> 00:04:51.312
♪ industrial electronic ♪

00:04:56.422 --> 00:04:58.866
Canvasing and going out without a map

00:04:58.866 --> 00:05:02.120
and just getting into
whatever situation you get into.

00:05:04.588 --> 00:05:06.268
♪ industrial electronic ♪

00:05:15.658 --> 00:05:17.515
From my experience in Ukrainian cities

00:05:17.515 --> 00:05:19.248
the looks of the buildings

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:23.729
usually drop pretty quickly
once you get out of the center

00:05:23.729 --> 00:05:25.577
but in Lviv here

00:05:25.577 --> 00:05:28.044
I've been walking for quite some time

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:29.509
and look at this.

00:05:29.987 --> 00:05:31.964
I did a long walk out of the center

00:05:31.964 --> 00:05:34.691
and just ended up
in this old wealthier neighborhood.

00:05:34.691 --> 00:05:35.846
It was beautiful.

00:05:35.846 --> 00:05:37.940
And so you can see
all the influences here.

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:40.153
All the influences in the architecture.

00:05:40.153 --> 00:05:41.513
[music continues]

00:05:42.182 --> 00:05:43.478
There's some art deco

00:05:44.088 --> 00:05:47.069
and then this Austrian-Hungarian style

00:05:47.069 --> 00:05:48.898
that's super impressive.

00:05:48.898 --> 00:05:51.426
I had no idea this existed in Ukraine.

00:05:51.459 --> 00:05:52.739
[birds chirping]

00:05:54.855 --> 00:05:56.535
[street car clanking]

00:06:07.974 --> 00:06:12.633
The history is absolutely [claps]
insane here.

00:06:12.706 --> 00:06:15.728
SOLOMIA: We had the
Austria-Hungarian Empire here.

00:06:15.728 --> 00:06:16.522
PETER: Right.

00:06:16.522 --> 00:06:18.048
SOLOMIA: In the early 20th century.

00:06:18.048 --> 00:06:21.843
Then 1914-1915 we had the Russians here.

00:06:21.843 --> 00:06:24.388
The Russian Imperial Army was here.

00:06:24.731 --> 00:06:26.665
Then the Austrians came back.

00:06:26.958 --> 00:06:28.973
Then after the First World War

00:06:28.973 --> 00:06:32.397
we had the Proclamation
of Ukrainian Independence.

00:06:32.397 --> 00:06:34.917
It was the Western Ukrainian
People's Republic

00:06:34.917 --> 00:06:38.359
that then joined the
Ukrainian People's Republic

00:06:38.621 --> 00:06:41.896
and then we had the
Polish-Ukrainian War here.

00:06:41.896 --> 00:06:45.020
Pols took the area over
and they stayed here

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.867
until the beginning
of the Second World War.

00:06:47.867 --> 00:06:50.933
Then in 1939 the Soviets came here.

00:06:51.321 --> 00:06:53.099
Weren't the Nazis here for a little bit?

00:06:53.099 --> 00:06:54.845
-Yeah, in 1941.
-Right.

00:06:54.845 --> 00:06:56.208
SOLOMIA: The Nazis came here.

00:06:56.208 --> 00:06:57.566
They took the area over

00:06:57.566 --> 00:07:00.596
and they stayed here until 1944.

00:07:00.596 --> 00:07:04.350
Then in 1944 there was
the so-called liberation.

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:08.194
As the Soviets called it
but it was occupation for us.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:08.723
Right.

00:07:08.723 --> 00:07:09.983
And the Soviets stayed here

00:07:09.983 --> 00:07:13.508
until the collapse
of the Soviet Union in 1991.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:16.040
Wow.

00:07:16.552 --> 00:07:18.723
I never thought
a cemetery could be so beautiful.

00:07:18.723 --> 00:07:19.792
IVAN:  Yeah, yeah.

00:07:19.792 --> 00:07:23.954
SOLOMIA: A hundred years ago
they didn't have Instagram or Facebook.

00:07:23.954 --> 00:07:26.100
-How did they survive?
-[chuckles]

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:29.281
SOLOMIA: You know they wanted
everyone else to know

00:07:29.281 --> 00:07:31.172
that they were a rich family

00:07:31.172 --> 00:07:35.102
and so they bought
a very expensive plot of land

00:07:35.102 --> 00:07:36.782
on the cemetery.

00:07:37.003 --> 00:07:39.643
SOLOMIA: Then they built a family tomb

00:07:39.643 --> 00:07:44.934
and this way people could see
that the family had very high status

00:07:44.934 --> 00:07:47.713
in the society and they were respected.

00:07:48.123 --> 00:07:50.722
So this is like 17th century...

00:07:50.722 --> 00:07:53.356
Instagram or Facebook,
yeah if you look at it.

00:07:53.356 --> 00:07:54.356
Here we go.

00:07:55.578 --> 00:07:58.875
PETER: That would be the person with
like a million followers or something?

00:07:58.875 --> 00:08:00.919
Probably even more I would say.

00:08:00.919 --> 00:08:04.631
-So it's the same...
-More expensive than a Downtown villa.

00:08:05.056 --> 00:08:06.736
♪ driving techno ♪

00:08:07.167 --> 00:08:10.307
I absolutely love the murals here.

00:08:10.307 --> 00:08:12.215
They're so beautiful

00:08:12.215 --> 00:08:15.396
and many people from this part
of the world don't like the murals

00:08:15.396 --> 00:08:17.095
'cause they're associated with communism

00:08:17.095 --> 00:08:20.157
and they have a message behind them

00:08:20.157 --> 00:08:24.705
but as an outsider I'm not connected
to them politically at all.

00:08:24.705 --> 00:08:26.411
So I just see a beautiful mural.

00:08:26.756 --> 00:08:27.796
Look at that.

00:08:28.725 --> 00:08:29.725
[exhales]

00:08:30.597 --> 00:08:33.130
-That's Soviet isn't it?
-It is Soviet.

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:36.080
SOLOMIA: And it's good.

00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:37.520
♪ driving techno ♪

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.020
[streetcar clanking]

00:08:54.809 --> 00:08:57.676
IVAN: Yay
PETER: Oh that's cool, look a that.

00:08:58.448 --> 00:08:59.404
[door closes]

00:08:59.404 --> 00:09:01.084
♪ heavy metal guitar ♪

00:09:07.765 --> 00:09:11.093
SOLOMIA: Concrete jungle,
that's the area where I live.

00:09:12.103 --> 00:09:15.126
From a tourist viewpoint
it might be interesting to go there

00:09:15.126 --> 00:09:19.038
and snap all the Soviet tower blocks

00:09:19.353 --> 00:09:22.304
but being an insider living there

00:09:22.304 --> 00:09:24.489
it's not the best experience.

00:09:24.489 --> 00:09:26.169
[heavy metal continues]

00:09:34.268 --> 00:09:35.796
[men playing football]

00:09:39.773 --> 00:09:41.750
PETER: It's super safe feeling.

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:43.657
I haven't met one panhandler.

00:09:43.657 --> 00:09:45.088
I don't know if I've been lucky

00:09:45.088 --> 00:09:47.825
but nobody's come up to me
and asked for anything

00:09:47.825 --> 00:09:52.316
and I haven't seen one person
sleeping on the streets.

00:09:53.612 --> 00:09:56.914
Like no homeless people
and they have to exist for sure.

00:09:56.914 --> 00:09:59.681
It's interesting that this is
somewhat of a tourist city

00:09:59.681 --> 00:10:02.909
and usually when that's the case

00:10:03.414 --> 00:10:06.315
there are a lot of people
bumming for money

00:10:06.315 --> 00:10:08.185
or sleeping on the streets

00:10:08.185 --> 00:10:09.630
and I haven't seen it here.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.807
So I'm curious,
do all those people get removed

00:10:11.807 --> 00:10:14.026
and pushed outside of the center?

00:10:14.026 --> 00:10:15.466
I don't know the story.

00:10:15.466 --> 00:10:17.687
Ukraine's not the richest country
on the planet

00:10:17.687 --> 00:10:21.158
and to see none of that
is really interesting

00:10:21.158 --> 00:10:25.443
'cause you'll see way more of it
in Europe in general than you will here.

00:10:25.443 --> 00:10:28.661
Homeless people,
it's pretty interesting because they...

00:10:28.661 --> 00:10:31.912
They will help you or show you around.

00:10:31.912 --> 00:10:33.590
They are trying to be helpful

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:37.475
-not just ask you for money for nothing.
-Right.

00:10:37.907 --> 00:10:42.377
-They don't come off as homeless.
-Seriously I haven't seen one beggar...

00:10:42.377 --> 00:10:44.464
-or homeless person here.
-It is true.

00:10:44.464 --> 00:10:45.744
Which is bizarre.

00:10:46.506 --> 00:10:49.578
Look at that pink Hummer,
how ugly is that thing?

00:10:49.612 --> 00:10:50.972
Well, it happens.

00:10:51.181 --> 00:10:53.429
PETER: No not her, this pink Hummer.

00:10:53.429 --> 00:10:54.767
[laughing]

00:10:55.456 --> 00:10:57.589
IVAN: Sorry, it's my judgmental nature.

00:10:59.618 --> 00:11:01.250
I love the sounds here.

00:11:01.250 --> 00:11:03.564
I like hearing those rail cars go by.

00:11:03.564 --> 00:11:04.690
There's something in that.

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:06.290
[streetcar clanking]

00:11:11.437 --> 00:11:14.615
But also the nature,
especially in these parks.

00:11:15.189 --> 00:11:17.967
They're very lively, lots of birds.

00:11:17.967 --> 00:11:19.167
Lots of just...

00:11:19.413 --> 00:11:20.822
Maybe it's 'cause it's spring

00:11:20.822 --> 00:11:27.143
but if feels like there's a good fusion
with the natural and the urban here.

00:11:27.839 --> 00:11:29.572
♪ serene ♪
[birds chirping]

00:11:53.033 --> 00:11:57.364
I swear to God there are
more older couples in love here

00:11:57.569 --> 00:11:59.067
than pretty much anywhere else.

00:11:59.067 --> 00:12:01.786
I've seen so many couples, older couples

00:12:01.786 --> 00:12:04.550
holding hands, walking these streets

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:06.180
and smiling at each other.

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:10.481
I think there are a lot of
good family values

00:12:10.481 --> 00:12:12.925
and just a lot of values in general

00:12:12.925 --> 00:12:15.334
and maybe it's because
it's chiller here and more relaxed

00:12:15.334 --> 00:12:17.865
and people have more time for each other
but it seems like...

00:12:19.845 --> 00:12:22.287
A lot of the old people
have it sort of figured out.

00:12:22.287 --> 00:12:23.967
[serene music continues]

00:12:28.042 --> 00:12:31.434
[music fades into choir singing]

00:12:36.426 --> 00:12:38.848
Look at these cool guys here in Lviv.

00:12:38.848 --> 00:12:40.128
CHILD: Yeah boy.

00:12:41.060 --> 00:12:42.180
[all laughing]

00:12:43.887 --> 00:12:45.007
♪ deep piano ♪

00:12:56.257 --> 00:12:57.561
Super cool city.

00:12:57.561 --> 00:13:01.094
I just scratched the surface
here for three days

00:13:01.581 --> 00:13:06.071
but from my outside eyes
I was highly impressed.

00:13:06.578 --> 00:13:08.702
If you haven't been here
definitely come here.

00:13:08.702 --> 00:13:10.382
If you're from here...

00:13:11.458 --> 00:13:13.434
You're in a cool place,
you're in a cool city.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:15.240
I was impressed.

00:13:15.439 --> 00:13:18.103
That's my story on Lviv.

00:13:18.171 --> 00:13:20.922
It was absolutely fantastic.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.030
[piano continues]

